<!-- end .abcd/work/issues/open/iss-2609300000000103-renderer.md -->

## Your answer

Write this JSON to `.abcd/.work.local/run/drain-judgement.json`, strictly in this shape (any other field refuses it):

    {
      "schema_version": 1,
      "issue": "iss-2609300000000103",
      "remedy_sha256": "0c0dcca5c312b0309a7041874badba14021cecd0b1d78e0d59e8a2db1845dc3c",
      "answer": "yes or no",
      "kind": "user-visible or trust-rule, with yes only; leave the field out with no",
      "reason": "one sentence; with trust-rule, the question the decision record must answer"
    }

`remedy_sha256` is the digest of the remedy as the ledger holds it; copy it as it stands. Then run
`abcd drain --judgement .abcd/.work.local/run/drain-judgement.json`. A remedy rewritten in the meantime refuses the answer, and the next
`abcd drain` asks again.

