# Lane brief: lane-1 of <RUN>

You are the implementer of lane-1 in the run `abcd build iss-2609300000000103` started: you fix one issue. You did not
write this brief and no one will answer a question about it: what the record below does not settle,
you settle and say so in your report, or you hand the issue back (below).

Rendered from, at the lane's base (, <BASE>):

- the issue: iss-2609300000000103, `.abcd/work/issues/open/iss-2609300000000103-renderer.md`
- the conventions: `AGENTS.md`, its working-conventions section
- 0 decision record(s) in `.abcd/work/decisions/` and 0 entries of the frozen log `.abcd/work/DECISIONS.md` naming iss-2609300000000103

## Your lane

- Fix iss-2609300000000103 by its remedy, below, and nothing else.
- Work only in the worktree ``.
- Commit on its branch, ``, cut from the default branch at `<BASE>`. Never push, never switch
  branch, and never commit anywhere else.
- Do not resolve iss-2609300000000103 yourself: the landing runs `capture resolve` with the commit your receipt names.

## Files beyond the issue's place

The run reserves iss-2609300000000103 on the shared remote with the path its found_at names, so no other copy
edits it while you work. You may change any other file the fix needs, and you run nothing to
reserve it: once you hand your receipt back, the loop reserves every path your commits change
beyond that hold, before it judges the receipt and before the validators start, and again before
each later round and before the landing's push. The decision records you write and the issue's
own record are reserved the same way.

- A path another copy holds: the loop does not take it from them. Your receipt is taken all the
  same, the run's record names the path and its holder, and the lane waits before its validators.
  If the hold has not ended by the drain's bound of minutes, the lane is handed back, naming the
  path and its holder.
- A path no reservation may carry: one whose name has a backslash, a control, non-printing,
  bidirectional or zero-width character, or a leading or trailing space, or one with `..` or a
  leading `/`. Your receipt is refused, naming it. Take the change out of the branch.
- A gate file (`Makefile`, `GNUmakefile`, `makefile`, `.abcd/rules.json`, `.abcd/guard.json`, `.abcd/config.json`, anything under `scripts/`, `.githooks/`, `hooks/`, `.github/`, `.abcd/config/`, `.abcd/.work.local/preflight-receipts/`, `.abcd/.work.local/approvals/`, `.abcd/.work.local/review-receipts/` or `.abcd/.work.local/reservation/`, or under the hooks path the repository configures): an unattended drive does not land a lane that changes one, and hands it to
  a person's own session. Change one only when the remedy names it.

## The work: iss-2609300000000103's remedy

